 "equipment_type": "Power meter (power analyzer)",
 "applies_to": "Circutor CVM-C10, CVM-C11, CVM-B100, CVM-B150 and CVM-E3-MINI panel power analyzers with BACnet communications.",
 "summary": "These Circutor power analyzers share one BACnet object map: 50 Analog Inputs for per-phase and three-phase voltage, current, power, power factor, THD, energy (consumed and generated) and maximum demand, plus three Analog Values for the MS/TP address, baud rate and device instance. They talk BACnet MS/TP over RS-485; the CVM-C11 Ethernet model can run BACnet IP instead.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet MS/TP",
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": "CVM-C10: BACnet available from device version 3.00",
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "The same object table (AI 0-49, AV 1-3) is printed in the CVM-C10 (M001B01-03-23A), CVM-C11 (M361B01-03-25A) and CVM-B100/B150 (M010B01-03-26A) manuals. The CVM-E3-MINI manual (M170B01-03-25B) prints it without AI 39 NeutralCurrent.",
  "BACnet IP is only on the CVM-C11-ITF-IN-ETH-ICT2 Ethernet model (Ethernet protocol set to BACnet IP, UDP 47808); the others are BACnet MS/TP only.",
  "The PICS has no read/write column. AIs are read-only; the manual says the AV address, baud and ID objects can be written.",
  "Object names are kept as printed, including Ph2NU1-3 for the phase-to-neutral voltages and MaxDemand_kVA (printed with a line break after the underscore in some manuals).",
  "Units here are the printed symbols; the manual prints I_AVG and In in the units column for AI 38 and AI 39 (amps)."
 ],
 "source": {
  "title": "CVM-C10 Power analyzer Instruction Manual (section 4.10.5 PICS map)",
  "doc_number": "M001B01-03-23A",
  "revision_date": null,
